00:16:37,246 --> 00:16:38,076
Torque it over!

267
00:16:38,159 --> 00:16:38,989
Yeah, right!

268
00:16:39,072 --> 00:16:39,902
That's mine!

269
00:16:39,985 --> 00:16:40,815
Screw you!

270
00:16:40,898 --> 00:16:41,728
I found it!

271
00:16:41,811 --> 00:16:43,117
You're gonna break it, you idiots!

272
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:44,030
That's cool, man!

273
00:16:44,113 --> 00:16:45,942
I just wanna cash it in for you!

274
00:16:46,100 --> 00:16:46,930
Yeah, right!

275
00:16:47,160 --> 00:16:49,042
Come on, just give me one pearl!

276
00:16:57,380 --> 00:16:58,210
Back off!

277
00:17:01,300 --> 00:17:02,917
You can only blame yourself.

278
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:05,941
Next time, let's try this
without all the running.

279
00:17:06,580 --> 00:17:07,840
Look what I found!

280
00:17:08,540 --> 00:17:09,500
No way!

281
00:17:09,840 --> 00:17:11,040
Get back here!

282
00:17:13,760 --> 00:17:14,590
Thief!

283
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:21,230
Hey!

284
00:17:21,313 --> 00:17:22,440
Move it, you brat!

285
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:25,460
What is your problem?

286
00:17:25,860 --> 00:17:27,380
You want some of this?

287
00:17:27,700 --> 00:17:29,080
He went that way!

288
00:17:35,840 --> 00:17:36,670
Samo!

289
00:17:36,753 --> 00:17:37,874
Hey, are you up there?

290
00:17:40,140 --> 00:17:41,980
Oh, what's up, Ace?

291
00:17:42,840 --> 00:17:44,657
Sorry, I'm a little late this time.

292
00:17:44,740 --> 00:17:45,858
More than a little.

293
00:17:45,980 --> 00:17:49,220
I went out there and made
a killing already today.

294
00:17:51,940 --> 00:17:52,980
Oh, yeah?

295
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:55,860
Well, maybe I did, too. Let's see.

296
00:17:56,980 --> 00:17:58,360
Whoa, dude!

297
00:17:58,720 --> 00:17:59,955
You got more than me!

298
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:02,960
That's a ton of cash. What happened?

299
00:18:03,720 --> 00:18:07,661
Some chumps near the gate, robbed
them blind and made a run for it.

300
00:18:07,840 --> 00:18:08,860
Well, crap.

301
00:18:09,300 --> 00:18:10,888
Guess you win again, buddy.

302
00:18:11,080 --> 00:18:13,077
It doesn't matter if you win or lose.

303
00:18:13,160 --> 00:18:16,120
We've got five years of
pirate savings piled up.

304
00:18:16,480 --> 00:18:18,539
We should both be happy about that.

305
00:18:22,440 --> 00:18:23,920
We worked pretty hard.

306
00:18:25,080 --> 00:18:26,280
Yeah, no kidding.

307
00:18:27,740 --> 00:18:32,357
We'll leave this stump behind and go
places these chumps never even dreamed of.

308
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:35,480
This is all gonna be
worth it. Just you wait.

309
00:18:42,080 --> 00:18:43,727
We'd better put it away now.

310
00:18:43,820 --> 00:18:45,677
We can't let anyone else see this.

311
00:18:45,760 --> 00:18:47,100
So how much is a ship?

312
00:18:47,360 --> 00:18:50,197
I want a good one, but it
seems like we're pretty rich.

313
00:18:50,280 --> 00:18:52,180
Yeah, could take ten million.

314
00:18:52,460 --> 00:18:53,500
Maybe even more.

315
00:18:54,020 --> 00:18:54,850
Shouldn't rush it.

316
00:18:54,933 --> 00:18:56,580
Did you say ship?

317
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,700
You're gonna be pirates?

318
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:01,214
And you've got hidden treasure already?

319
00:19:01,320 --> 00:19:03,080
I'm gonna be a pirate too!

320
00:19:14,800 --> 00:19:16,000
Shut up!

321
00:19:19,280 --> 00:19:20,440
Know what's cool?

322
00:19:20,640 --> 00:19:23,537
Now that I know where you go,
I can follow you every day!

323
00:19:23,620 --> 00:19:24,450
Great!

324
00:19:25,320 --> 00:19:26,180
Luffy, huh?

325
00:19:26,620 --> 00:19:28,973
This is the brat you were talking about.

326
00:19:29,340 --> 00:19:31,497
Does that mean you told
your friends about me?

327
00:19:31,580 --> 00:19:34,177
I was telling my friend
how annoying you were.

328
00:19:34,260 --> 00:19:37,220
He also told me that your
head's full of rocks.

329
00:19:38,560 --> 00:19:39,520
Head rocks!

330
00:19:39,760 --> 00:19:42,397
You do realize we're messing
with you here, right?

331
00:19:42,480 --> 00:19:45,068
The route I took here
wasn't easy to follow.

332
00:19:45,240 --> 00:19:48,577
I knew he was hard-headed, but
I didn't think he was so tough.

333
00:19:48,660 --> 00:19:51,072
So great that Ace has other friends, too!

334
00:19:51,200 --> 00:19:52,917
I bet we're all gonna be best pals!

335
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:54,220
I'm not your pal.

336
00:19:54,480 --> 00:19:56,537
You don't even know my name, stupid.

337
00:19:56,620 --> 00:19:58,440
Okay, then what is your name?

338
00:19:58,620 --> 00:19:59,960
It's, uh, a secret.

339
00:20:00,880 --> 00:20:02,440
I told you, didn't I?

340
00:20:02,580 --> 00:20:03,837
You need to live here.

341
00:20:03,920 --> 00:20:08,685
The mountains made you tough, but at this
rate, our whole plan's gonna be ruined.

342
00:20:08,780 --> 00:20:09,610
What now?

343
00:20:11,540 --> 00:20:12,900
He knows our secret.

344
00:20:13,280 --> 00:20:15,751
We can't trust him to keep his mouth shut.

345
00:20:15,980 --> 00:20:17,100
He's too stupid.

346
00:20:23,180 --> 00:20:24,160
We'll kill him.

347
00:20:24,440 --> 00:20:26,200
Yep, sounds good.

348
00:20:31,240 --> 00:20:32,680
Stop, this is scary!

349
00:20:33,780 --> 00:20:34,960
Somebody help me!

350
00:20:35,600 --> 00:20:36,776
I don't want to die!

351
00:20:37,040 --> 00:20:39,177
Give me a break, this kid is the worst!

352
00:20:39,260 --> 00:20:41,297
Just kill him already, hurry it up!

353
00:20:41,380 --> 00:20:43,337
He's your problem, what are you doing?

354
00:20:43,420 --> 00:20:45,757
Because I've never killed
anyone before, okay?

355
00:20:45,840 --> 00:20:47,037
Well, neither have I!

356
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:48,537
I don't know how this crap works!

357
00:20:48,620 --> 00:20:51,437
Just don't throw me in the
water, I'm begging you!

358
00:20:51,520 --> 00:20:52,760
Okay, the river!

359
00:20:53,020 --> 00:20:55,357
That's convenient, but
why did he say that?

360
00:20:55,440 --> 00:20:56,577
I told you, he's stupid!

361
00:20:56,660 --> 00:20:57,920
Somebody help me!

362
00:20:59,120 --> 00:20:59,950
That's enough!

363
00:21:02,660 --> 00:21:03,740
Don't kill me!

364
00:21:05,140 --> 00:21:06,020
Wait, listen.

365
00:21:06,180 --> 00:21:07,777
I just heard some screaming.

366
00:21:07,860 --> 00:21:09,657
Son of a kid! Ah, damn it!

367
00:21:09,740 --> 00:21:11,840
Somebody hurt him! Set him free.

368
00:21:12,020 --> 00:21:13,497
We gotta get out of here and fast.

369
00:21:13,580 --> 00:21:17,051
If people start snooping around,
they'll find our treasure.

370
00:21:18,600 --> 00:21:21,017
Sounds like you're talking
about Ace and Sabo.

371
00:21:21,100 --> 00:21:23,159
Those two are infamous around here.

372
00:21:23,380 --> 00:21:25,262
And the one who took your money.

373
00:21:25,540 --> 00:21:26,677
That was Ace, right?

374
00:21:26,760 --> 00:21:28,557
The kid who had the black hair, you said?

375
00:21:28,640 --> 00:21:29,470
Uh-huh.

376
00:21:29,553 --> 00:21:31,177
This is real pathetic, I know.

377
00:21:31,260 --> 00:21:32,640
We both got sloppy.

378
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:34,360
He's either cocky or dumb.

379
00:21:34,920 --> 00:21:38,137
You can't rob pirates blind
and expect to get away with it.

380
00:21:38,220 --> 00:21:40,517
Bottom line is, if we
don't get that money back?

381
00:21:40,600 --> 00:21:42,457
Captain Blue Jam's gonna skin us alive!

382
00:21:42,540 --> 00:21:43,775
and I mean literally.

383
00:21:45,400 --> 00:21:47,180
Blue Jam? Crap!

384
00:21:47,400 --> 00:21:49,837
How was I supposed to know
they were working with him?

385
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:51,260
You robbed those guys?

386
00:21:51,480 --> 00:21:53,437
Are you trying to get us killed or what?

387
00:21:53,520 --> 00:21:56,240
Yeah, this is not gonna end well.

388
00:21:56,740 --> 00:22:00,328
That sword looks sharp, though
you probably saw that already.

389
00:22:01,200 --> 00:22:03,120
The guy with him is porching me.

390
00:22:03,380 --> 00:22:04,340
He's crazy.

391
00:22:05,460 --> 00:22:09,780
Lose a fight with him, and he'll scalp
you alive just to hear you scream.

392
00:22:13,520 --> 00:22:16,000
Just lay low and let him pass by for now.

393
00:22:17,600 --> 00:22:19,280
Uh-oh, he's gone.

394
00:22:21,740 --> 00:22:26,152
You better put me down right now, you
big - How did you get caught already?

395
00:22:26,660 --> 00:22:28,280
Who the hell is this?

396
00:22:28,480 --> 00:22:30,068
This guy won't put me down!

397
00:22:30,160 --> 00:22:31,140
Ace, help!

398
00:22:32,800 --> 00:22:34,517
Ace, why aren't you saving me?

399
00:22:34,600 --> 00:22:35,430
We're friends, right?

400
00:22:35,513 --> 00:22:36,857
We should have killed him.

401
00:22:36,940 --> 00:22:38,500
No, we're all dead. Help!

402
00:22:40,060 --> 00:22:42,040
So, you know Ace, do you?

403
00:22:43,420 --> 00:22:44,397
Yeah, that's right.

404
00:22:44,480 --> 00:22:47,304
And if you cry, do you
think he'll come for you?

405
00:22:48,860 --> 00:22:50,507
Yeah, because we're friends.

406
00:22:51,540 --> 00:22:54,246
Except he just tried to
kill me, so maybe not.

407
00:22:55,360 --> 00:22:56,190
Shut up.

408
00:22:56,273 --> 00:22:57,560
Are you kidding me?

409
00:22:58,460 --> 00:23:00,917
If he's your friend,
maybe you can help us.

410
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:02,437
See, Ace stole our money.

411
00:23:02,520 --> 00:23:05,814
And if we got it back, we
wouldn't have to hurt anybody.

412
00:23:06,020 --> 00:23:08,667
You don't happen to know
where it is, do you?

413
00:23:13,420 --> 00:23:14,500
We're screwed.

414
00:23:14,720 --> 00:23:18,426
They're gonna take our treasure
for sure for once in your life.

415
00:23:18,540 --> 00:23:19,370
Please shut up

416
00:23:32,160 --> 00:23:33,940
What a crappy lawyer?

417
00:23:38,320 --> 00:23:41,720
All right fine, I'm sure you just forgot.

418
00:23:45,780 --> 00:23:48,720
Don't worry, I have ways
of jogging your memory.

419
00:23:50,380 --> 00:23:52,020
I told you, I don't know!

420
00:23:52,200 --> 00:23:53,847
Let go of me, you dumb jerk!

421
00:23:54,140 --> 00:23:56,357
He's gonna kick your
butt, I'm telling you!

422
00:23:56,440 --> 00:23:57,499
You're a big jerk!

423
00:23:57,980 --> 00:23:59,340
Okay, so now what?

424
00:23:59,620 --> 00:24:01,920
Stop asking me, you know what!

425
00:24:10,660 --> 00:24:11,940
Let me go! No!

426
00:24:12,400 --> 00:24:14,720
I'm not telling you a dark thing!

427
00:24:22,440 --> 00:24:23,920
You little punk!

428
00:24:38,360 --> 00:24:42,677
The Gum-Gum fruit turned me into rubber,
so that stuff's not going to work on me.

429
00:24:42,760 --> 00:24:43,740
Calm down.

430
00:24:45,380 --> 00:24:46,960
A Devil Fruit, huh?

431
00:24:47,620 --> 00:24:48,450
Hmm.

432
00:24:48,940 --> 00:24:50,880
I know how to deal with that.

433
00:24:53,340 --> 00:24:55,220
Bring me my pair of gloves.

434
00:24:56,120 --> 00:24:56,950
Yes, sir!

435
00:24:57,720 --> 00:24:59,140
Hurry, man! Faster!

436
00:24:59,400 --> 00:25:01,097
We're screwed if those guys come back!

437
00:25:01,180 --> 00:25:03,945
We gotta move all this,
but I don't know where.

438
00:25:04,600 --> 00:25:08,057
Luffy's pretty stubborn, but it's only
a matter of time before he rats us out.

439
00:25:08,140 --> 00:25:11,657
I'm not losing our pirate savings
to those jerks or anyone else.

440
00:25:11,740 --> 00:25:13,877
It took us five years to score all this.

441
00:25:13,960 --> 00:25:16,254
We can't get stuck in this dump forever

442
00:25:21,060 --> 00:25:25,317
I'll try to clear this up a little the
money a stole isn't just some chump

443
00:25:25,400 --> 00:25:28,857
change It's a matter of life and death
for me and all of my buddies here,

444
00:25:28,940 --> 00:25:31,440
and you're gonna tell me where it is

445
00:25:32,360 --> 00:25:34,540
Even if I gotta beat it out of you

446
00:25:36,200 --> 00:25:37,060
Well not

447
00:25:45,840 --> 00:25:46,760
That's rough.

448
00:25:50,760 --> 00:25:52,020
I'm warning you, kid.

449
00:25:52,160 --> 00:25:53,807
You don't piss off a pirate.

450
00:25:53,980 --> 00:25:58,627
If I don't kick your ass, Captain Blue
Jam's gonna kill you and all of us, too.

451
00:26:05,740 --> 00:26:06,897
Let me go!

452
00:26:06,980 --> 00:26:08,440
You're hurting me!

453
00:26:08,940 --> 00:26:10,000
Somebody help!

454
00:26:13,220 --> 00:26:15,697
We don't have time to
stand around, you idiots.

455
00:26:15,780 --> 00:26:18,577
Go look for Ace and Sabo
while I take care of this one.

456
00:26:18,660 --> 00:26:19,490
Yes, sir!

457
00:26:27,980 --> 00:26:29,440
Ace and Sabo, huh?

458
00:26:29,680 --> 00:26:30,740
Yeah, I know him.

459
00:26:31,100 --> 00:26:32,260
Oh, I get it.

460
00:26:32,400 --> 00:26:33,635
You're from the city.

461
00:26:34,560 --> 00:26:35,977
Leave those two be.

462
00:26:36,060 --> 00:26:38,236
If you were locals, you'd understand.

463
00:26:38,540 --> 00:26:41,100
They may be kids, but they're also crazy.

464
00:26:41,340 --> 00:26:44,437
Yeah, man, they got claws like
a tiger if you cross them.

465
00:26:44,520 --> 00:26:45,820
A sensabo, huh?

466
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:47,040
I wouldn't know.

467
00:26:48,020 --> 00:26:50,497
But while we're all
having this little chat,

468
00:26:50,580 --> 00:26:53,240
why don't you always
fork over your wallets?

469
00:26:53,440 --> 00:26:55,040
We don't want any trouble.

470
00:26:55,300 --> 00:26:56,653
We'll ask someone else.

471
00:27:00,640 --> 00:27:02,875
Didn't realize it was getting so late.

472
00:27:03,380 --> 00:27:05,180
All right, I finally did it!

473
00:27:05,420 --> 00:27:07,596
Not even Luffy knows about this spot!

474
00:27:11,220 --> 00:27:12,050
I'm back!

475
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:15,140
I moved everything. What happened?

476
00:27:15,360 --> 00:27:17,713
Are they poking around at the old place?

477
00:27:19,800 --> 00:27:21,420
No, that's the thing.

478
00:27:21,940 --> 00:27:24,587
Blue Jam's guys are
still out looking for us!

479
00:27:24,740 --> 00:27:26,152
And what does that mean?

480
00:27:26,280 --> 00:27:27,927
I'm telling you, it's Luffy!

481
00:27:29,240 --> 00:27:31,887
All that time and he
still didn't rat us out!

482
00:27:33,100 --> 00:27:36,757
I thought he would since he's
such an idiot that Andy was

483
00:27:36,840 --> 00:27:39,617
crying whenever we left him
But you know what this means,

484
00:27:39,700 --> 00:27:40,530
don't you?

485
00:27:40,613 --> 00:27:42,044
They're torturing him right now

486
00:27:43,680 --> 00:27:45,560
What if he still doesn't talk

487
00:27:54,400 --> 00:27:56,420
Getting awful late, isn't it?

488
00:27:57,280 --> 00:27:59,640
Who did I leave in charge today?

489
00:28:00,920 --> 00:28:04,391
Well, Captain Blue Jam, if I
recall, it should be Porchemy.

490
00:28:05,440 --> 00:28:07,087
Huh, then he'd better hurry.

491
00:28:08,700 --> 00:28:11,080
Well, surely they made the sale.

492
00:28:11,660 --> 00:28:13,900
It couldn't have taken him that long.

493
00:28:14,720 --> 00:28:18,980
Maybe Porchemy thinks he's clever
enough to take my money and skip town.

494
00:28:19,240 --> 00:28:20,593
Of course not, Captain.

495
00:28:20,920 --> 00:28:24,626
I doubt he would throw his life
away over some measly treasure.

496
00:28:26,220 --> 00:28:27,420
Let's hope not.

497
00:28:32,400 --> 00:28:33,600
Come on, kid.

498
00:28:33,820 --> 00:28:34,720
Spit it out.

499
00:28:38,860 --> 00:28:39,920
Wait. Wait.

500
00:28:40,360 --> 00:28:41,419
Portrume, stop it.

501
00:28:41,520 --> 00:28:43,461
I don't think he's going to talk.

502
00:28:46,780 --> 00:28:47,920
He's shutting down.

503
00:28:48,180 --> 00:28:50,768
The kid's not even
calling for help anymore.

504
00:28:54,540 --> 00:28:56,837
If he wasn't going to talk,
he would have done it already.

505
00:28:56,920 --> 00:29:00,097
And to be honest, this is
getting kind of hard to watch.

506
00:29:00,180 --> 00:29:02,298
Show the little bastards some mercy!

507
00:29:05,560 --> 00:29:09,897
If you have time to bitch about this,
then you have time to go look for Ace!

508
00:29:09,980 --> 00:29:13,920
We're the ones who are gonna get
killed here, not the damn kid!

509
00:29:14,260 --> 00:29:15,380
Save your breath,

510
00:29:15,540 --> 00:29:19,540
cause you'll be begging for mercy
from Captain Blue Jam soon enough!

511
00:29:24,360 --> 00:29:25,717
They're gonna kill that child.

512
00:29:25,800 --> 00:29:28,637
Do you think we should call
the sheriff from the city?

513
00:29:28,720 --> 00:29:29,720
There's no point.

514
00:29:29,960 --> 00:29:32,837
I mean, this place doesn't
fall under any country's laws.

515
00:29:32,920 --> 00:29:36,297
Plus, that portrait me guy's a
member of the Blue Jam Pirates.

516
00:29:36,380 --> 00:29:38,733
They're paying off the nobles, you know.

517
00:29:39,360 --> 00:29:42,537
So in other words, even if they
do get arrested for a crime,

518
00:29:42,620 --> 00:29:44,537
they're just gonna be pardoned in the end.

519
00:29:44,620 --> 00:29:47,920
Besides, what's one more dead
body in a place like this?

520
00:29:48,240 --> 00:29:49,420
Nobody gives a damn.

521
00:29:51,160 --> 00:29:51,990
Answer me!

522
00:29:53,780 --> 00:29:55,320
I'm not talking.

523
00:29:56,260 --> 00:29:57,620
You little punk!

524
00:29:57,860 --> 00:30:01,095
I'll beat that secret out of
you or I'll beat you dead!

525
00:30:04,900 --> 00:30:06,000
Tell me!

526
00:30:09,620 --> 00:30:11,460
I won't do it!

527
00:30:12,220 --> 00:30:13,860
I won't talk!

528
00:30:14,380 --> 00:30:15,900
Just let me go!

529
00:30:19,640 --> 00:30:21,760
I'm not telling you!

530
00:30:24,540 --> 00:30:25,370
Fine.

531
00:30:25,453 --> 00:30:26,283
Enough of this.

532
00:30:44,320 --> 00:30:46,397
We're finished here, brat.

533
00:30:46,480 --> 00:30:47,600
Whoa!

534
00:30:48,720 --> 00:30:50,220
Let him go!

535
00:31:01,600 --> 00:31:02,560
Forge me!

536
00:31:02,840 --> 00:31:03,980
It's that damn kid!

537
00:31:04,200 --> 00:31:06,040
He's got the money, that brat!

538
00:31:06,660 --> 00:31:07,490
Huh?

539
00:31:08,080 --> 00:31:10,020
Ace, you're here!

540
00:31:15,600 --> 00:31:17,300
Thanks for showing up, kid.

541
00:31:17,500 --> 00:31:19,029
You saved us some trouble.

542
00:31:19,420 --> 00:31:20,877
Your friend ain't squealing.

543
00:31:20,960 --> 00:31:21,937
He's pretty tough.

544
00:31:22,020 --> 00:31:24,340
But I think you'll talk. Ace!

545
00:31:24,600 --> 00:31:25,980
Sa-Savo!

546
00:31:26,840 --> 00:31:27,740
Do it!

547
00:31:32,100 --> 00:31:33,380
Boss, are you okay?

548
00:31:36,660 --> 00:31:37,490
Ace!

549
00:31:37,960 --> 00:31:38,790
Sabo!

550
00:31:38,873 --> 00:31:39,739
That kind of hurt.

551
00:31:40,020 --> 00:31:41,940
Who hit me? You?

552
00:31:43,740 --> 00:31:46,328
You punks don't get who
you're messing with.

553
00:31:46,520 --> 00:31:47,991
Yeah, you're all dead me!

554
00:31:48,580 --> 00:31:50,140
Shut your mouth and fight!

555
00:31:50,660 --> 00:31:52,960
Sabo, help Luffy! You guys!

556
00:31:54,140 --> 00:31:57,640
One thing, that ugly dude
has a sword. Be careful.

557
00:32:10,260 --> 00:32:11,200
No way!

558
00:32:11,540 --> 00:32:14,069
Orange of me, that
other kid got our knife!

559
00:32:17,000 --> 00:32:18,471
Quick, make a run for it!

560
00:32:19,040 --> 00:32:20,140
You go ahead.

561
00:32:20,740 --> 00:32:21,570
What?

562
00:32:21,653 --> 00:32:23,380
Ace, let's just leave!

563
00:32:23,740 --> 00:32:27,200
I don't run from my enemies. Ever. Got it?

564
00:32:28,140 --> 00:32:31,580
And I don't go easy on
my enemies. Come on!

565
00:32:31,740 --> 00:32:33,077
These guys aren't just thugs.

566
00:32:33,160 --> 00:32:34,437
They're Blue Jam Pirates!

567
00:32:34,520 --> 00:32:35,991
Yeah, you got that right.

568
00:32:36,540 --> 00:32:39,017
Now, I'm done playing games here.

569
00:32:39,100 --> 00:32:41,337
You've got something that belongs to us.

570
00:32:41,420 --> 00:32:43,780
Be good and give it back you brat

571
00:32:44,460 --> 00:32:47,477
You're just a kid, and I don't
blame you for acting stupid,

572
00:32:47,560 --> 00:32:50,031
but fork over the cash or you'll regret it

573
00:32:52,180 --> 00:32:53,937
We've got better plans for it.

574
00:32:54,020 --> 00:32:55,196
That's our money now

575
00:32:58,820 --> 00:33:01,340
Then you are dead hold on a sec.

576
00:33:01,460 --> 00:33:02,519
I'll be right back

577
00:33:03,880 --> 00:33:05,580
That's enough of this crap

578
00:33:10,360 --> 00:33:12,660
I'm not going to lose, you hear?

579
00:33:12,960 --> 00:33:15,100
I'd rather just kill myself.

580
00:33:15,260 --> 00:33:16,700
Not if we do it first!

581
00:33:17,600 --> 00:33:19,560
Come at me, you pricks!

582
00:33:28,680 --> 00:33:31,500
I heard the whole damn story, Porchemy.

583
00:33:32,000 --> 00:33:33,580
You should be ashamed.

584
00:33:33,940 --> 00:33:37,280
Did you seriously get
beaten by a couple of kids?

585
00:33:38,220 --> 00:33:39,050
Yeah.

586
00:33:39,133 --> 00:33:40,660
Forgive me, Captain.

587
00:33:41,520 --> 00:33:42,420
The money.

588
00:33:42,660 --> 00:33:43,997
I've heard enough of this.

589
00:33:44,080 --> 00:33:45,668
You're not fit for my crew.

590
00:33:57,360 --> 00:33:59,620
Ace, that was really not cool.

591
00:33:59,840 --> 00:34:01,700
Those guys were actual pirates.

592
00:34:02,040 --> 00:34:03,500
Next time, we run.

593
00:34:03,740 --> 00:34:06,437
Whatever your deal is,
it's not worth dying over.

594
00:34:06,520 --> 00:34:07,557
This sucks.

595
00:34:07,640 --> 00:34:09,280
I like my old one better.

596
00:34:11,960 --> 00:34:13,660
We made a huge mistake.

597
00:34:13,980 --> 00:34:15,517
Pissing off pirates like that.

598
00:34:15,600 --> 00:34:17,737
Man, they probably told their captain.

599
00:34:17,820 --> 00:34:19,477
What are we supposed to do now?

600
00:34:19,560 --> 00:34:20,900
That was scary!

601
00:34:21,280 --> 00:34:23,180
I thought I was gonna die!

602
00:34:26,740 --> 00:34:28,120
Would you shut up?

603
00:34:28,220 --> 00:34:31,057
You're not hurt that bad,
so stop crying already!

604
00:34:31,140 --> 00:34:32,957
When are you gonna stop being a baby?

605
00:34:33,040 --> 00:34:34,687
Don't you wanna be a pirate?

606
00:34:37,900 --> 00:34:38,920
Thank you.

607
00:34:43,000 --> 00:34:43,830
You...

608
00:34:45,100 --> 00:34:46,500
You saved me.

609
00:34:47,100 --> 00:34:48,980
Stop it! Calm down.

610
00:34:49,360 --> 00:34:50,654
He's just happy, okay?

611
00:34:54,340 --> 00:34:56,100
All right. What gives?

612
00:34:56,280 --> 00:34:58,217
Why didn't you tell them what they wanted?

613
00:34:58,300 --> 00:35:00,697
You think they wouldn't kill
you because you're a kid?

614
00:35:00,780 --> 00:35:02,486
Those guys don't give a damn.

615
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:04,240
I was afraid.

616
00:35:04,820 --> 00:35:05,650
I...

617
00:35:05,733 --> 00:35:09,137
but you wouldn't be my
friend. Yeah? Well, so what?

618
00:35:09,220 --> 00:35:10,717
That still beats dying, right?

619
00:35:10,800 --> 00:35:12,797
Besides, why do you want to be my friend?

620
00:35:12,880 --> 00:35:13,710
That's dumb.

621
00:35:16,440 --> 00:35:17,270
Because...

622
00:35:17,353 --> 00:35:18,998
It's not like I've been nice to you.

623
00:35:19,160 --> 00:35:21,557
In fact, I've been giving
you hell ever since we met.

624
00:35:21,640 --> 00:35:22,497
It's been months.

625
00:35:22,580 --> 00:35:24,345
Why haven't you just given up?

626
00:35:30,800 --> 00:35:35,017
Well, cause, cause I, I
got no one else to turn to?

627
00:35:35,100 --> 00:35:37,817
I can't go back to Windmill Village.

628
00:35:37,900 --> 00:35:39,917
I don't like the mountain bandits either.

629
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:43,157
I'd be all alone all the
time if I didn't follow you!

630
00:35:43,240 --> 00:35:47,280
Getting beat up hurts, but
being lonely hurts more.

631
00:35:48,560 --> 00:35:49,880
Alone? Why?

632
00:35:50,520 --> 00:35:52,080
Gramps is all I have

633
00:35:53,700 --> 00:35:55,680
You feel better around me?

634
00:35:56,020 --> 00:35:56,920
Uh-huh.

635
00:35:57,680 --> 00:36:00,380
Otherwise, you feel lonely? Uh-huh.

636
00:36:03,140 --> 00:36:05,520
Do I think Gold Roger had a kid?

637
00:36:07,320 --> 00:36:10,820
If he did, then too bad for
that poor runt. No kidding.

638
00:36:11,020 --> 00:36:12,357
They'd put him to death.

639
00:36:12,440 --> 00:36:14,880
He'd probably deserve it, too, I bet.

640
00:36:20,960 --> 00:36:24,220
Do you think I deserve to live?

641
00:36:27,720 --> 00:36:29,220
Of course I do!

642
00:36:30,740 --> 00:36:31,780
I see.

643
00:36:34,620 --> 00:36:36,160
But you're still annoying.

644
00:36:36,500 --> 00:36:38,500
Weak little crybabies piss me off.

645
00:36:40,920 --> 00:36:42,220
I'm not weak.

646
00:36:42,400 --> 00:36:43,459
I'm really strong.

647
00:36:44,000 --> 00:36:44,830
Ha!

648
00:36:44,913 --> 00:36:46,217
You think you're really strong?

649
00:36:46,300 --> 00:36:48,837
You were crying your eyes out
the whole time you were tied up.

650
00:36:48,920 --> 00:36:51,597
Have you ever gotten hit
by a spiky thing that big?

651
00:36:51,680 --> 00:36:53,137
I'm just seven years old.

652
00:36:53,220 --> 00:36:55,477
Wait till I turn ten
years old like you guys,

653
00:36:55,560 --> 00:36:58,317
and then I'll be stronger
and won't cry anymore.

654
00:36:58,400 --> 00:37:00,557
Age has nothing to do with it, you brat.

655
00:37:00,640 --> 00:37:02,577
Hell, when I was seven, I was tough.

656
00:37:02,660 --> 00:37:03,490
So what?

657
00:37:03,573 --> 00:37:05,297
I'm gonna be so tough, you're gonna cry.

658
00:37:05,380 --> 00:37:07,657
I promised, Shanks, I'd
be a great pirate someday,

659
00:37:07,740 --> 00:37:09,257
and that means way greater than you.

660
00:37:09,340 --> 00:37:10,717
Ha, you'll be a crappy pirate.

661
00:37:10,800 --> 00:37:12,660
Nuh-uh. Yeah, huh? Nuh-uh.

662
00:37:14,860 --> 00:37:16,400
Okay, enough of that.

663
00:37:17,720 --> 00:37:18,550
Geez.

664
00:37:18,660 --> 00:37:22,920
Now listen, in case you guys forgot,
we got a problem here. A problem?

665
00:37:24,420 --> 00:37:27,817
This forest where I've been living
is awfully close to their hideout,

666
00:37:27,900 --> 00:37:29,080
the Cove of Pirates.

667
00:37:29,300 --> 00:37:31,537
What if one night I'm a little too tired,

668
00:37:31,620 --> 00:37:34,502
sleep a little too hard,
and they sneak up on me?

669
00:37:36,040 --> 00:37:37,700
So, I need your help.

670
00:37:53,520 --> 00:37:55,226
What's with all the bandages?

671
00:37:55,560 --> 00:37:58,089
Have they been fighting
bears or something?

672
00:38:00,120 --> 00:38:02,160
That's not the problem.

673
00:38:06,320 --> 00:38:08,760
Hey, boss, come quick.

674
00:38:08,980 --> 00:38:10,120
This isn't good.

675
00:38:10,840 --> 00:38:12,546
Give me a second, it's early.

676
00:38:13,060 --> 00:38:13,890
Huh?

677
00:38:14,060 --> 00:38:14,890
Ahh!

678
00:38:14,973 --> 00:38:16,536
What have those brats been up to now?

679
00:38:16,940 --> 00:38:18,920
One, two...

680
00:38:19,760 --> 00:38:20,590
Huh?

681
00:38:21,660 --> 00:38:24,480
Hey, Slave, who's that other kid with you?

682
00:38:26,060 --> 00:38:27,320
Who's what now?

683
00:38:30,820 --> 00:38:33,580
Ugh, two brats is already too many!

684
00:38:33,820 --> 00:38:35,055
Who the hell are you?

685
00:38:35,820 --> 00:38:37,040
You mean me?

686
00:38:39,020 --> 00:38:40,260
Ugh, right.

687
00:38:40,880 --> 00:38:42,600
Hi, I'm Sabo.

688
00:38:43,280 --> 00:38:44,110
Huh?

689
00:38:44,193 --> 00:38:46,400
Ace's friend, I see. Oh, good.

690
00:38:46,640 --> 00:38:48,640
It's like I'm already living here.

691
00:38:48,880 --> 00:38:50,177
And you must be Dadan, right?

692
00:38:50,260 --> 00:38:51,090
Hiya!

693
00:38:51,220 --> 00:38:54,977
You're just as worthless as those
other two low-lifes mushing off me.

694
00:38:55,060 --> 00:38:55,890
Oh, yeah?

695
00:38:55,973 --> 00:38:59,135
Well, I heard that you're a
worthless old hag yourself.

696
00:39:09,360 --> 00:39:11,020
Luffy! Ace! Sabo!

697
00:39:11,200 --> 00:39:12,847
There aren't any free rides!

698
00:39:13,000 --> 00:39:16,471
You twerps better be grateful
and get to work this instant!

699
00:39:16,700 --> 00:39:18,320
You got it, thank you!

700
00:39:29,100 --> 00:39:33,960
Fearing for his life, Sabo left Gray
Terminal and found a home with Ace and Luffy,

701
00:39:34,300 --> 00:39:35,940
much to Dedan's dismay.

702
00:39:36,760 --> 00:39:40,460
For the three unwanted guests,
it was a never-ending party.

703
00:39:41,060 --> 00:39:44,060
Making any excuse to get
out of their daily chores,

704
00:39:44,380 --> 00:39:46,657
they hunted wild animals in the mountains,

705
00:39:46,740 --> 00:39:50,975
tussled with hooligans in the city,
and dueled with pirates of the cove.

706
00:39:51,680 --> 00:39:52,620
Within time,

707
00:39:53,060 --> 00:39:55,877
news of their wild exploits
reached far and wide,

708
00:39:55,960 --> 00:39:59,666
even over the high walls surrounding
the center of the kingdom.
